The {C1,C2} Black subgroup has exactly two liberties at B1/B2. White cannot legally occupy either, as both placements are immediate self-atari (B2 has no liberties after the move, being adjacent solely to A2/B3/C2; symmetrically for B1). No other candidate point initiates a forcing sequence that captures any Black group against every possible reply.

